      <div type="clause" n="27.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 27.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>E l’autre meited, s’il est trové dedenz sache e soche, si perderad la femme, e le seinur l’averad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>E l’altre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.1"/> meited<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.2"/>, s’il est trové dedenz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.3"/> sache et soche, sil perdra la femme, et le seignour<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.4"/> l’averad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>Et alteram medietatem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.a"/>, nisi inueniatur in terra eius qui habet soch et sac etc.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.b"/>, quia tunc uxor perdet et dominus habebit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="27.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="266" ed="#robertson"/>E l'autre meited, s'il est trové dedenz sache e soche, si perderad la femme e le seinur l'averad.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>27, 1. Jedoch wenn es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.de.1"/> in [einem mit] Jurisdiction [privilegirten Bezirk] gefunden wird, so soll die Frau die eine Hälfte verlieren und der [Gerichtsbarkeits]herr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_27-1.lnote.de.2"/> sie erhalten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">27, 1. But if it is found in [a district] with jurisdiction [privileges], then the wife shall lose the one half and the [jurisdictional] lord receive it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="267" ed="#robertson"/>And with regard to the other half, if the theft is discovered in a district over which the lord has rights of jurisdiction, the wife shall lose her share and it shall pass to the lord.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 266–267 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 512–513, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">labor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">labor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">merted <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> metted <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">merted <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> metted <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dedanz <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dedanz <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nor Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">denke</hi> nur dann <hi rend="italic">hinzu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply ‘only then’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">L denkt die anderen Privilegien oben</hi> 2, 3 (<hi rend="italic">hier unpassend</hi>) <hi rend="italic">hinzu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">L supplies the other privileges of 2, 3 above (inappropriate here)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">290</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘sie’ (die Habe; Schmid), sondern der Diebstahl</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘sie’ (the property; Schmid), but the theft</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_27-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">290</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Offenbar derselbe eine wie in 27</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Evidently the same one as in 27</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
